<title>USA: Motorola to provide modems in South Korea.</title>
<headline>Motorola to provide modems in South Korea.</headline>
<dateline>ARLINGTON HEIGHTS, Ill. 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Motorola Inc's Multimedia Group said Thursday it was selected to provide cable modems to Korea Electric Power Data Network Co, a wholly owned subsidiary of the South Korean utility company Korea Electric Power Corp.</p>
<p>Korea Electric will use Motorola's cable modems to establish broadband services over its two-way hybrid fiber-coaxial network, currently covering 70 percent of South Korea.</p>
<p>The value of the contract was not disclosed.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
